{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:58b809c8fe47a3f9","name":"HAVw A5 Juggernaut","source":{"id":"source:reference-58b809c8fe47a3f9","title":"HAVw A5 Juggernaut","revision":19460,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:01:07Z","sha256":"5542bfac7d6b84dabee09b21b04fba1aad2e51b6d457483a3b435a5adedeed4a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19460","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=HAVw%20A5%20Juggernaut&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-58b809c8fe47a3f9","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Smaller and older than the ",{"tag":"a","children":["HAVw A6 Juggernaut"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/HAVw_A6_Juggernaut?action=edit&redlink=1"}," that dominated the battlefields of closing days of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"},", the A5 Juggernaut is a 10-wheeled, heavily armored assault vehicle that continues to see use in many Imperial forces despite its age. Wherever an ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-AT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-AT","referenceId":"reference:72b76e7d76526ae5"}," or similar heavy walker isn't available, an A5 is used as a replacement. Though faster than an ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-AT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-AT","referenceId":"reference:72b76e7d76526ae5"},", the A5 is less maneuverable (especially in rough terrain), slightly less resistant to damage, and requires a larger crew. It also mounts slightly lighter weapons, and it lacks the power generation to upgrade to lasers as powerful as those on an ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-AT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-AT","referenceId":"reference:72b76e7d76526ae5"},". Despite these shortcomings, an A5 is a dangerous and versatile combat vehicle. It can effectively spearhead a ground assault, act as a mobile command center, engage in hit-and-run raids, and even act as an anti-aircraft battery when engaging ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," or low-flying ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though the Empire owns more A5s than anyone else, as the years pass and the Empire retires and replaces them, other groups begin picking them up. Many Imperial A5s are left as smoking wrecks on battlefields, and while it's not worth the Empire's time or money to recover and repair them, crime cartels, major corporations, and insurgent groups are willing to go to much greater lengths to acquire such a powerful ground unit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["HAVw A5 Juggernaut Statistics (CL 11)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wheeled Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wheeled_Vehicle"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[